  <article class="page-content">
    <h1>How to apply a live wallpaper</h1>
    <p>A live wallpaper is a short looping video. A website can't set your device background directly — no browser allows that, on any platform — so after downloading, you'll use one built-in setting or a small free app to finish the job. Pick your device below.</p>

    <div class="guide-platform reveal">
      <h2>Android</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Download the <strong>phone</strong> version of the live wallpaper from its page.</li>
        <li>Some Android phones (One UI, MIUI, and others) let you set a video directly: open <strong>Settings → Wallpaper</strong>, choose <strong>Live wallpaper</strong> or <strong>Video wallpaper</strong>, then select the downloaded file.</li>
        <li>If your phone doesn't offer that option, install a free app such as <strong>Video Live Wallpaper</strong> from the Play Store, open it, and point it at the downloaded video.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="guide-platform reveal">
      <h2>iPhone</h2>
      <p>iOS only animates wallpapers that are set up as a <strong>Live Photo</strong> (a paired image + short video), not a plain downloaded video file. To use a Klipmo live wallpaper on iPhone:</p>
      <ol>
        <li>Download the <strong>phone</strong> version of the live wallpaper.</li>
        <li>Use a free "video to Live Photo" converter app from the App Store to convert the downloaded file into a Live Photo, and save it to your Photos.</li>
        <li>Go to <strong>Settings → Wallpaper → Add New Wallpaper → Live</strong>, choose the converted photo, and set it.</li>
        <li>On the lock screen, a live wallpaper animates with a long-press; on the home screen it stays static — that's an iOS limitation, not a Klipmo one.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="guide-platform reveal">
      <h2>Windows</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Download the <strong>laptop</strong> version of the live wallpaper.</li>
        <li>Install <strong>Lively Wallpaper</strong> (free, open-source) from its official site or the Microsoft Store.</li>
        <li>Open Lively, choose <strong>Add wallpaper</strong>, and select the downloaded video file. It will loop as your desktop background.</li>
        <li>If you'd rather use <strong>Wallpaper Engine</strong> on Steam (a popular paid option), import the video the same way from its wallpaper library.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="guide-platform reveal">
      <h2>Mac</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Download the <strong>laptop</strong> version of the live wallpaper.</li>
        <li>macOS doesn't support custom video wallpapers natively. Install a small free app such as <strong>Plash</strong> (runs a video or web page as your desktop background) from its official site.</li>
        <li>Open the app, load the downloaded video, and set it to run at login if you want it to persist across restarts.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>

    <p>None of these apps are made by Klipmo — they're independent tools that read a video file and apply it as a background. Always download apps from their official source (App Store, Play Store, Microsoft Store, or the developer's own site).</p>
  </article>
